{"name":"Holy Water","hex":"#466e77","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"holy water","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["In certain Christian churches, water that has been sanctified by a priest or bishop for the purpose of baptism or for the blessing of persons, places, or things."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/holy_water"}],"entries":[{"title":"Holy water","blocks":[{"text":"Holy water is water that has been blessed by a member of the clergy or a religious figure, or derived from a well or spring considered holy. The use for cleansing prior to a baptism and spiritual cleansing is common in several religions, from Christianity to Sikhism. The use of holy water as a sacramental for protection against evil is common among Catholics, Eastern Christians, and some Protestants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/A_Thai_student_pouring_Holy_water.jpg/330px-A_Thai_student_pouring_Holy_water.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holy_water"},{"title":"Holy Water (We the Kingdom album)","blocks":[{"text":"Holy Water is the debut studio album by American contemporary Christian music band We the Kingdom, which was released via Capitol Christian Music Group on August 7, 2020. The album features guest appearance by Bethel Music, Tasha Cobbs Leonard, Maverick City Music, and Bear Rinehart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ac/Holy_Water_by_We_the_Kingdom_%28Official_Album_Cover%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holy_Water_(We_the_Kingdom_album)"},{"title":"Water","blocks":[{"text":"Water is an inorganic compound with the chemical formula H2O. It is a transparent, tasteless, odorless, and nearly colorless chemical substance. It is the main constituent of Earth's streams, lakes, and oceans. Water is also the fluid of all known living organisms, in which it acts as a solvent. Water, being a polar molecule, undergoes strong intermolecular hydrogen bonding which is a large contributor to its physical and chemical properties. It is vital for all known forms of life, despite not providing food energy or being an organic micronutrient. Due to its presence in all organisms, its chemical stability, its worldwide abundance, and its strong polarity relative to its small molecular size, water is often referred to as the \"universal solvent\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/H2O_2D_labelled.svg/330px-H2O_2D_labelled.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/A_Thai_student_pouring_Holy_water.jpg/500px-A_Thai_student_pouring_Holy_water.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/A_Thai_student_pouring_Holy_water.jpg/1280px-A_Thai_student_pouring_Holy_water.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/A_Thai_student_pouring_Holy_water.jpg/500px-A_Thai_student_pouring_Holy_water.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Thai student pouring the holy water on his two hands at Erawan shrine, Bangkok","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_Thai_student_pouring_Holy_water.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/1880_photograph_of_the_Golden_Temple%2C_Darbar_Sahib%2C_sacred_pool_and_nearby_buildings%2C_Amritsar.jpg/500px-1880_photograph_of_the_Golden_Temple%2C_Darbar_Sahib%2C_sacred_pool_and_nearby_buildings%2C_Amritsar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/co